.TH RUN-NVIDIA 1 "October 2026" "run-nvidia" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
run-nvidia \- run a command with NVIDIA PRIME Render Offload
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B run-nvidia
.RI [ -- ] " command " [ args... ]
.br
.B run-nvidia
.RB [ -h | --help ]
.br
.B run-nvidia
.RB [ -V | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B run-nvidia
executes a command after setting the environment variables commonly used for
NVIDIA PRIME Render Offload:
.PP
.nf
__NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1
__GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia
__VK_LAYER_NV_optimus=NVIDIA_only
.fi
.PP
The wrapper then replaces itself with the requested command using
.BR execvp (3).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.B --
Stop option parsing and treat the next argument as the command.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run Firefox using the NVIDIA GPU:
.PP
.nf
run-nvidia firefox
.fi
.PP
Inspect the OpenGL renderer:
.PP
.nf
run-nvidia glxinfo -B
.fi
.PP
Launch a Vulkan diagnostic tool:
.PP
.nf
run-nvidia vulkaninfo
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
When the requested command starts successfully,
.B run-nvidia
is replaced by that command, so the command's own exit status is observed.
If setup fails, run-nvidia exits with status 1. Invalid usage returns 2.
A missing command returns 127; other execution failures return 126.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A correctly installed NVIDIA driver and working PRIME Render Offload setup are
required for GPU offloading to function.
